(2989140, 421105, 61679, '<td valign="top">Back to comment:  You aren''t using the full size limit that the challenges allow for an image.  Your image is 350 X 234 pixels in size.  You are allowed to make the longest dimension 640 pixels.  You are also allowed a file size of 150 kb.  Your image is only 100 kb.  Smaller images and smaller file sizes make it harder to see the detail in your image.  I initially gave this a 4 for being small but I am bumping to a 6 because it has so much personality.  If it was bigger, I would probably score it even higher.</td>', 'Back to comment:  You aren''t using the full size limit that the challenges allow for an image.  Your image is 350 X 234 pixels in size.  You are allowed to make the longest dimension 640 pixels.  You are also allowed a file size of 150 kb.  Your image is only 100 kb.  Smaller images and smaller file sizes make it harder to see the detail in your image.  I initially gave this a 4 for being small but I am bumping to a 6 because it has so much personality.  If it was bigger, I would probably score it even higher.', '2006-11-02 12:43:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(2989152, 420932, 3102, '<td valign="top">Just amazing.  In addition to the furry coat, she''ll be wearing a ribbon at the end of the week, I''m sure!</td>', 'Just amazing.  In addition to the furry coat, she''ll be wearing a ribbon at the end of the week, I''m sure!', '2006-11-02 12:47:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2989158, 420603, 61679, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: Your image shows a lot of personality but the lighting looks a little harsh on the face.  Maybe a different B&amp;W conversion technique would help keep the details in her face.  Take a look at this great <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=43" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tuitorial</a> on B&amp;W conversion.</td>', 'Back to comment: Your image shows a lot of personality but the lighting looks a little harsh on the face.  Maybe a different B&W conversion technique would help keep the details in her face.  Take a look at this great tuitorial on B&W conversion.', '2006-11-02 12:49:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2989164, 420664, 61679, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: This image doesn''t show a lot of personality, as it looks like you sneaked the shot and then cropped it to make a portrait.  The face has a very flat look to it and I think a different B&amp;W conversion technique would help bring out the details in her face.  Take a look at this great <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=43" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tuitorial</a> on B&amp;W conversion.  The focus also looks a little soft around the eyes.  Did you remember to sharpen the image after downsizing it for the challenge?</td>', 'Back to comment: This image doesn''t show a lot of personality, as it looks like you sneaked the shot and then cropped it to make a portrait.  The face has a very flat look to it and I think a different B&W conversion technique would help bring out the details in her face.  Take a look at this great tuitorial on B&W conversion.  The focus also looks a little soft around the eyes.  Did you remember to sharpen the image after downsizing it for the challenge?', '2006-11-02 12:51:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2989172, 421068, 61679, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: Sorry but this is more of a candid than a portrait in my opinion.  The background is very cluttered and the crop indicates that you weren''t ready for this event to happen.  Your image would benefit from post processing work using levels or curves to bring out the couple better.</td>', 'Back to comment: Sorry but this is more of a candid than a portrait in my opinion.  The background is very cluttered and the crop indicates that you weren''t ready for this event to happen.  Your image would benefit from post processing work using levels or curves to bring out the couple better.', '2006-11-02 12:54:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2989178, 419270, 61679, '<td valign="top">Back to comment:  Man, I think you would have had a killer shot here if the clown hadn''t raised his/her arms.  The out of focus elbow in front of the face is killing this image.</td>', 'Back to comment:  Man, I think you would have had a killer shot here if the clown hadn''t raised his/her arms.  The out of focus elbow in front of the face is killing this image.', '2006-11-02 12:56:19.000000', NULL, 1),
