(3009782, 418781, 30049, '<td valign="top">Nice work in eliminating that background and letting the ''Little Lady'' shine thru.  It''s a tad thin on landscape orientation - yes, it fits, but the ratio isn''t typical.  That''s ust a minor nit.  This is a photograph that she will treasure years from now, and that should be a large part of having a portrait taken - yes?  Overall, nicely done.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Nice work in eliminating that background and letting the ''Little Lady'' shine thru.  It''s a tad thin on landscape orientation - yes, it fits, but the ratio isn''t typical.  That''s ust a minor nit.  This is a photograph that she will treasure years from now, and that should be a large part of having a portrait taken - yes?  Overall, nicely done.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-07 09:13:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3009786, 421141, 30049, '<td valign="top">Nice job with the soft focus look, yet keeping him and the horse sharp.  Some intrigue/interest to the viewer wondering what the distraction to the left is for ''The Paso Man''.  I naturally want to see this cropped some off the left, but with them both looking left it would cramp the photo.  This photograph begs to be in portrait mode.  I can see the perfect crop from here.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Nice job with the soft focus look, yet keeping him and the horse sharp.  Some intrigue/interest to the viewer wondering what the distraction to the left is for ''The Paso Man''.  I naturally want to see this cropped some off the left, but with them both looking left it would cramp the photo.  This photograph begs to be in portrait mode.  I can see the perfect crop from here.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-07 09:16:18.000000', NULL, 1),
