(3014453, 421056, 3214, '<td valign="top">Fantastic work.  And there will always be cretins, it''s the nature of "art appreciation".  And too dark, uncalibrated monitors.  As long as ya average over 7 across the challenge, what''s to worry about?</td>', 'Fantastic work.  And there will always be cretins, it''s the nature of "art appreciation".  And too dark, uncalibrated monitors.  As long as ya average over 7 across the challenge, what''s to worry about?', '2006-11-08 12:59:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3014457, 419889, 3214, '<td valign="top">Congrats, Judi!  I like the unforced expression (at least on the human''s part...) and how the hair frames her face--probably better so in BW than in color?</td>', 'Congrats, Judi!  I like the unforced expression (at least on the human''s part...) and how the hair frames her face--probably better so in BW than in color?', '2006-11-08 13:02:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3014467, 420804, 3214, '<td valign="top">Met the challenge better than anybody IMO, and sadly under-rated.  I would have probably masked and painted out the details of the shirt''s texture near his cheek with a very slight blur to bring the attention more completely to his compelling face.</td>', 'Met the challenge better than anybody IMO, and sadly under-rated.  I would have probably masked and painted out the details of the shirt''s texture near his cheek with a very slight blur to bring the attention more completely to his compelling face.', '2006-11-08 13:05:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3014476, 419889, 50231, '<td valign="top">Congrats Judi! This is such a sweet shot! Funny that we both used our girls and our cats, except my girl is my fiance but still. Great minds ...<br/> <br/>:-)</td>', 'Congrats Judi! This is such a sweet shot! Funny that we both used our girls and our cats, except my girl is my fiance but still. Great minds ... :-)', '2006-11-08 13:07:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3014488, 418364, 3214, '<td valign="top">Daring man, entering a primate in a "portrait" challenge, as it has seemed to me in the past that DPCers think portrait = Human.  Gorgeous work, great comp and emotion.</td>', 'Daring man, entering a primate in a "portrait" challenge, as it has seemed to me in the past that DPCers think portrait = Human.  Gorgeous work, great comp and emotion.', '2006-11-08 13:09:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3014567, 418442, 65603, '<td valign="top">This is a pic taken while contemplating a divorce. It is the real feeling caught on camera. I agree the white in the foreground was a little much. Thanx for all the feed back.</td>', 'This is a pic taken while contemplating a divorce. It is the real feeling caught on camera. I agree the white in the foreground was a little much. Thanx for all the feed back.', '2006-11-08 13:33:24.000000', NULL, 0),
