(3015900, 417474, 44886, '<td valign="top">Hey guys... thanks a lot for the comments. I feel pretty stupid for realizing I cropped her fingers out!!!. How did I not notice...? Ohhh well. My mistake... <br/>I selected the wrong camera on the post... <br/>It''s taken with a Pentax *ist DS with the kit lens.</td>', 'Hey guys... thanks a lot for the comments. I feel pretty stupid for realizing I cropped her fingers out!!!. How did I not notice...? Ohhh well. My mistake... I selected the wrong camera on the post... It''s taken with a Pentax *ist DS with the kit lens.', '2006-11-08 19:33:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3015913, 421056, 66604, '<td valign="top">Wonderful photo. This is going on my list of favorites. The expression on her face is lovely and the eyes adorable. Congratulations on this one and how in the world did you get 3 and 4 (or even 5 for that matter) scores I''ll never understand.</td>', 'Wonderful photo. This is going on my list of favorites. The expression on her face is lovely and the eyes adorable. Congratulations on this one and how in the world did you get 3 and 4 (or even 5 for that matter) scores I''ll never understand.', '2006-11-08 19:42:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3015936, 418201, 45475, '<td valign="top">Hmmm... I''m not really a cat person, but here goes: I like the selective desat(?) leaving the eyes that vivid colour. I think a tighter crop with the eyes dead center though, would have made more of an impact. Not sold on the editing around the edges, looks a little smudgy... which brings me back to wanting the tighter crop. Have to agree with Karma about needing a contrast boost too, or even a wee play with curves, just to give it some punch. Other than those issues, it''s not a bad pet portrait at all, but then it''s always going to be hard to compete against gorgeous human models... ;)</td>', 'Hmmm... I''m not really a cat person, but here goes: I like the selective desat(?) leaving the eyes that vivid colour. I think a tighter crop with the eyes dead center though, would have made more of an impact. Not sold on the editing around the edges, looks a little smudgy... which brings me back to wanting the tighter crop. Have to agree with Karma about needing a contrast boost too, or even a wee play with curves, just to give it some punch. Other than those issues, it''s not a bad pet portrait at all, but then it''s always going to be hard to compete against gorgeous human models... ;)', '2006-11-08 19:48:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3015941, 420025, 67547, '<td valign="top">Hey Kyle<br/>It''s uncle Jeff. How are you doing? Your dad said you had entered a picture and asked me to vote. I remember voting on your picture and thought it was very good. When I voted, I didn''t know it was yours. I only gave a few nines out and thats what I gave yours. I believe I commented on it also. I''m surprised that anyone would give it a 1, 2, or 3. Its way better then that. I wonder if some people vote low on all the pictures they think might give thiers competition...Anyways, great job and keep at it. You are on the right track.<br/>I plan on entering a few  challenges. I''m having trouble getting my pictures down to 150 kb. They get blurry. I''ll let you and your dad know when I get one entered.<br/>Stay in touch<br/>Jeff</td>', 'Hey KyleIt''s uncle Jeff. How are you doing? Your dad said you had entered a picture and asked me to vote. I remember voting on your picture and thought it was very good. When I voted, I didn''t know it was yours. I only gave a few nines out and thats what I gave yours. I believe I commented on it also. I''m surprised that anyone would give it a 1, 2, or 3. Its way better then that. I wonder if some people vote low on all the pictures they think might give thiers competition...Anyways, great job and keep at it. You are on the right track.I plan on entering a few  challenges. I''m having trouble getting my pictures down to 150 kb. They get blurry. I''ll let you and your dad know when I get one entered.Stay in touchJeff', '2006-11-08 19:51:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3015998, 421041, 42567, '<td valign="top">Great picture Erick...very cool with these two cats!</td>', 'Great picture Erick...very cool with these two cats!', '2006-11-08 20:15:41.000000', NULL, 0),
